Chapter: Parsmi--CheckHarness

 The compiler as a program that stops at the CHECK layer:
 `codexcheck < prog.codex 2> prog.check`.

 CodexIrHarness beside this one stops at the IR wire; this one stops one phase
 earlier, where the types are decided. What it buys is the same thing codexir
 buys and at the same pin: a second arm for the layer being built. The Rust
 checker has had exactly one gold -- `$CODEX_GOLDS/rungs/check.truth`, which is
 bare `fib`, ONE chapter, cut at 53b3b213 -- because the harness that produced
 it embeds its subject as a text literal and `parse-document` parses one
 chapter. Every real unit leads with ListUtils and Tuple, so the layer has been
 graded on a program shape it never actually meets.

 IT TAKES WHATEVER THE DRIVER TAKES. `compile-checked` is the driver's own
 phase, so a bare one-chapter file and a resolved multi-chapter unit both go
 through it unchanged -- and a program is fed here in the shape it is actually
 compiled in. `fib` cites nothing and uses neither tuples nor lists, so it is
 fed BARE: resolving it first prepends ListUtils and Tuple, which moves every
 number in this dump and answers a question nobody asked. Bare fib mints row
 ids up to 15; the same fib behind the two implicit chapters reaches 469.

 `type-bindings` IS `all-bindings`, WHICH IS BIGGER THAN IT LOOKS AND DOUBLE-
 COUNTS. It is `check-result.types & resolved-env`, so a chapter's own defs
 appear TWICE -- once inferred, once from the environment. For bare fib:

     257 builtins carrying a declared type
     +  3 fib's defs, in the environment
     +  3 fib's defs again, from check-result.types
     = 263

 Predicted from `Types/Builtins.codex` and measured on this binary; they agree.
 The eight builtins that declare no type -- True, False, Nothing, open-file,
 close-file, read-all, now, random-integer -- are the difference between that
 257 and the 265 names the table carries.

Section: Halt

 The same gate the other harnesses carry, in the same words, so a refusal
 compares as bytes rather than needing a reader that knows three formats.

  cc-halted : List Diagnostic -> Text
  cc-halted (es) =
   let n = list-length es
   in let e0 = list-at es 0
   in "CODEGEN-HALTED: " & show n & " error(s); no IR emitted; first CDX" & show (e0.code) & " " & (e0.message) & "\n"

Section: Kinds

 `type-kind` from the ladder's own CheckHarness, verbatim. The Rust side prints
 these words already, so keeping the spelling means the two dumps diff directly
 instead of through a translation table that could itself be wrong.

  cc-type-kind : CodexType -> Text
  cc-type-kind (t) =
   when t
    is IntegerTy (lo) (hi) (m) -> "int"
    is TextTy -> "text"
    is BooleanTy -> "bool"
    is CharTy -> "char"
    is ListTy (e) -> "list"
    is FunTy (p) (r) (q) -> "fn"
    is EffectfulTy (e) (s) (i) -> "eff"
    is ForAllTy (i) (b) -> "forall"
    is ForAllEff (c) (b) -> "foralleff"
    is TypeVar (i) -> "tvar"
    is SumTy (n) (a) (c) -> "sum:" & n.value
    is RecordTy (n) (a) (f) -> "rec:" & n.value
    is ConstructedTy (n) (a) -> "con:" & n.value
    is TypeCon (n) -> "tycon:" & n.value
    is otherwise -> "other"

  cc-bindings : List TypeBinding, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  cc-bindings (bs) (i) (len) = act
    if i >= len then print-line-uni "."
    else act
      let b = list-at bs i
      in print-line-uni ("tb " & (b.name) & " " & cc-type-kind (b.bound-type))
      cc-bindings bs (i + 1) len
    end
  end

Section: Driver

 `next-row-id` IS REPORTED AND THE LADDER'S HARNESS NEVER WAS. It is the
 counter behind the row variable in an effectful builtin's wire type --
 `print-line-uni` is `(fn text nothing (row (labels (label "Console.Write" ""))
 "" 460))` and that 460 is this number -- so it is the one figure that says
 whether a checker can emit an effectful type at all. Measured on the oracle:
 454 of `fib`'s 460 are minted before the subject's own code is reached, by the
 two implicit chapters every unit carries.

  opening : [Console, FileSystem] Nothing = act
    src <- read-file-uni "/dev/stdin"
    let mountain-base = init-phase-allocator
    in let deck-base = __heap-save
    in let deck-set = __deck-set deck-base
    in let deck-adv = __heap-advance 536870912
    in let checked = compile-checked src "Program" compile-flags-default
    in if bag-has-errors (checked.bag) then print-text (cc-halted (bag-errors (checked.bag)))
    else let bs = checked.all-bindings
    in let ust = checked.ust
    in act
      print-line-uni "--- check ---"
      print-line-uni ("check-errors " & show ((checked.bag).error-count))
      print-line-uni ("type-bindings " & show (list-length bs))
      cc-bindings bs 0 (list-length bs)
      print-line-uni ("substitutions " & show (list-length (ust.substitutions)))
      print-line-uni ("next-id " & show (ust.next-id))
      print-line-uni ("next-row-id " & show (ust.next-row-id))
      print-line-uni ("expr-types " & show (list-length (ust.expr-types)))
      print-line-uni "---"
    end
  end
